# Build-context filter. Secrets, production data and local tooling never reach
# the Docker daemon, so no cache layer can hold them.
#
# Rules (pinned by tests/unit/test_docker_build_context.py):
# - Exclude ONLY untracked paths. The builder stage runs
#   `git status --untracked-files=no` to count dirty files; an excluded TRACKED
#   path would look deleted there and inflate `dirty_files` in every image.
# - Keep `.git`: the builder (`source`) stage needs it to write
#   .build_info.json, then deletes it. The final stage never receives it.
# - The only negation allowed is `!.env.example`, so no later `!` line can
#   re-include something excluded above.
# This is the first layer. The second is the builder stage's `git clean -ffdx`,
# which drops any untracked file this list does not name.
.env*
!.env.example
.provision_state.json
certbot
backups
data
logs
profiles
.venv
.venv-test
venv
.superpowers
.claude
.notes
.playwright-mcp
docs/superpowers
.mutmut-cache
mutants
.pytest_cache
.ruff_cache
htmlcov
.coverage
build
dist
*.egg-info
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
.idea
.vscode
.build_info.json
.tools
